# deep_sky_objects.dat
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
#
# A list of the brightest deep-sky objects, which are visible to the naked eye
# or through binoculars, to be marked on the star wheel.
#
# Columns:
# 1. Label (underscores are turned into spaces)
# 2. Right ascension, J2000, hours
# 3. Declination, J2000, degrees
# 4. Type: G = galaxy; OC = open cluster; GC = globular cluster; N = nebula
# 5. Visual magnitude
# 6. Major axis, arcminutes
# 7. Minor axis, arcminutes
# 8. Position of the label relative to the symbol on northern planispheres:
#    below, above, left, right or centre (inside the symbol). These are
#    relative to the reading direction of the label, whose bottom faces the
#    centre of the star wheel. For labels on the left or right, a second line
#    (the common name) goes beneath the first, or above it with the suffix _up
#    (left_up, right_up).
# 9. Position of the label relative to the symbol on southern planispheres.

